# 12. Bare Repository vs Non-Bare Repository

## Bare Repository

* Used as a central repository.
* Stores only Git history.
* No working directory.
* Example: GitHub, GitLab, Bitbucket repositories.

## Non-Bare Repository

* Used by developers.
* Contains both the Git history and working directory.
* You can modify files, commit changes, and push updates.

